    {
      "id": 22005,
      "name": "TheJayMann",
      "username": "TheJayMann",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-08-28T19:13:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>If the deck were to not be removed, then it would continue playing one card during the play phase.  Any card that says “Omnitron does this” would not be valid as there is no Omnitron (even though it’s stated in the lore that Omnitron exists in all the devices he makes, this is not stated anywhere in the rules or the cards, so there is no Omnitron to do something).  The play a card at the end of turn, as well the draw a card from the trash at end of turn, are part of the Omnitron game text.  When Omnitron is removed, the gametext no longer exists, and thus no longer continue to play.  As well, the advance mode stuff goes away as it is no longer in play.  Given how complicated the results are, either “remove all villian cards except devices from play” has a slightly different meaning (not very good, as this will cause confusion), or an errata is needed, saying that all villain cards except device cards in play are removed from game (much clearer).  Unless, of course, all this extra complexity is desired.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:56:04.007Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
